BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Granny Squares 101 - August
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T143000
UID:bistitchual-9585295130882@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a Granny Squares 101 Course. The classes w
 ill be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday August 23rd from 12:30pm - 
 2:30pm Bring your yarn over and pull through to our two hour granny square
  class! From blankets\; to sweaters\; to bags\; and much more\, these cozy
  squares can be used in a wide range of designs. They’re a joy to make\,
  simple to reproduce and easy to customize to your own style and project n
 eeds. This class teaches how to make a basic granny square\, how to change
  colours and\, how to join squares together. We’ll discuss variations in
  construction and further possibilities. We expect students in this class 
 to already know how to chain\, make single and double crochets. You’ll n
 eed a 5.0 mm hook and worsted weight yarn in 2-3 colours. Materials are no
 t provided\, please bring your own or purchase these supplies at Bistitchu
 al with a 10% discount\, before class begins! Required materials: - worste
 d weight wool in a few different colours - 5.0mm hook Cancellation Policy 
 Classes must be paid for at the time of registration to reserve your spot.
  - If cancelled 48 hrs or more prior to the start of the class\, the order
  will be refunded. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start o
 f the class will not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/granny-squares-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Crochet - September
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260920T153000
UID:bistitchual-9533060808962@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a two session Beginner Crochet Course. The
  classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday September 20th an
 d 27th from 2:00pm-3:30pm Learn the fundamentals of crochet in this two pa
 rt class. We will be covering chaining and single crochet\, as well as dou
 ble and half-double crochets. Don’t know what any of that means? Great\,
  you’re in the right place! We’ll provide all the materials\, includin
 g a simple pattern that teaches you common terms and instructions you’ll
  encounter in most crochet projects. We will also discuss how to choose th
 e appropriate yarn and hook for a project as well as where you can take yo
 ur crafting after you master these basic techniques. There’s a lot to le
 arn\, and we’re excited to accompany your beginning in the wonderful cra
 ft of crochet! Materials are included! - 50g ball of worsted weight cotton
  in your choice of colour - 6mm crochet hook Our class size is capped at 4
  people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need. Mike will share
  lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. About the instru
 ctor: Tired of disposing of clothes that were still perfectly wearable\, M
 ike (he/him) started crafting mainly as a means of mending and repair. Thi
 s led him to knitting (and later crochet)\, which pretty much immediately 
 became one of his favourite tools of self-expression. Please note that cla
 sses will only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the mini
 mum is not met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. T
 here will be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your sp
 ot to let us know you are coming! Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid
  for at the time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 h
 rs or more prior to the start of the first class will be given a store cre
 dit. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class wi
 ll not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/beginner-crochet-september-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Knitting Course - September
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T133000
UID:bistitchual-9533059105026@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Knitting Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday September 13th
 \, 20th\, and 27th from 12-1:30pm Have you always wanted to learn to knit?
  We’ve got you covered! Beginner Knitting is a course for brand new begi
 nners\, and over these three 1.5hr classes\, Mike will teach you everythin
 g you need to create a basic project from beginning to end. Our class size
  is capped at 4 people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need. 
 Mike will share lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. (
 No experience necessary) Materials: Yarn and needles will be provided. Wha
 t We’ll Learn - How to make a slip knot. - Casting on. - The Knit stitch
 . - The Purl stitch. - Exploring Knit / Purl combinations. - Binding off. 
 - Weaving in ends. - Fixing common mistakes and how to avoid them. - Commo
 n uses of flat knitting. - Intro into Ravelry. Please note that classes wi
 ll only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minimum is 
 not met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. There wi
 ll be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spot to l
 et us know you are coming! About the instructor : Tired of disposing of cl
 othes that were still perfectly wearable\, Mike (he/him) started crafting 
 mainly as a means of mending and repair. This led him to knitting (and lat
 er crochet)\, which pretty much immediately became one of his favourite to
 ols of self-expression. Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at th
 e time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more
  prior to the start of the first class will be given a store credit. Class
 es cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will not be 
 reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/beginner-knitting-course-september-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
